Reproduced against `6e626ce7b64f57e61f3ff7757e36ce3addcd6ced` (fetched main), Node 24.19.0, with the repository lockfile and SDK 2026.11.4. Only synthetic input and temporary local trackers were used.

A source path accepted by `cite` can refer to the same file as a changed-source operand yet be silently excluded by `affected`. This produces a complete-looking empty impact report without reading the changed file.

Source:
- [sourceIdentity allows internal dot segments and repeated separators, and only removes one leading dot slash](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-evidence/blob/6e626ce7b64f57e61f3ff7757e36ce3addcd6ced/src/sources.ts#L8-L11).
- [affected compares changed paths with stored descriptor strings before checking the citation](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-evidence/blob/6e626ce7b64f57e61f3ff7757e36ce3addcd6ced/src/evidence.ts#L95-L110).

Reproduction:

```sh
review=$(mktemp -d)
git clone --quiet https://github.com/unbraind/pm-evidence.git "$review/package"
cd "$review/package"
git checkout --quiet 6e626ce7b64f57e61f3ff7757e36ce3addcd6ced
npm ci --ignore-scripts --no-audit --no-fund
npm run build
cat > repro-path.mjs <<'JS'
import assert from 'node:assert/strict';
import { mkdtemp, mkdir, writeFile } from 'node:fs/promises';
import { tmpdir } from 'node:os';
import { join } from 'node:path';
import { PmClient } from '@unbrained/pm-cli/sdk';
import { cite, affected, check } from './dist/index.js';
const root = await mkdtemp(join(tmpdir(), 'evidence-review-'));
const workspace = join(root, 'tracker');
const client = new PmClient({ cwd: root, pmRoot: workspace, author: 'fixture', noExtensions: true });
await client.init('fixture', { defaults: true, agentGuidance: 'skip', mergeFence: false });
await client.config('project', 'set', 'agent_identity.probes_enabled', 'false');
const { item } = await client.create({ type: 'Task', title: 'Source path review', createMode: 'progressive' });
const options = { root, workspace, author: 'fixture' };
await mkdir(join(root, 'docs'));
await writeFile(join(root, 'docs', 'sample.txt'), 'before\nold value\nafter');
await cite(item.id, 'docs/./sample.txt', { ...options, selector: { kind: 'lines', start: 2, end: 2 } });
await writeFile(join(root, 'docs', 'sample.txt'), 'before\nnew value\nafter');
const full = await affected(options);
const filtered = await affected({ ...options, changed: ['docs/sample.txt'] });
assert.equal(full.rows.length, 1); assert.equal(full.rows[0].freshness, 'changed'); assert.equal(filtered.rows.length, 0); assert.equal(filtered.receipt.sourceComplete, true);
console.log(JSON.stringify({ fullRows: full.rows.length, fullFreshness: full.rows[0].freshness, filteredRows: filtered.rows.length, filteredReads: filtered.receipt.verification.sourceReads, filteredComplete: filtered.receipt.complete, filteredSourceComplete: filtered.receipt.sourceComplete }));
JS
node repro-path.mjs
```

Observed output:

```json
{"fullRows":1,"fullFreshness":"changed","filteredRows":0,"filteredReads":0,"filteredComplete":true,"filteredSourceComplete":true}
```

Expected: a citation to docs/./sample.txt is included when the changed-file list contains docs/sample.txt, or the noncanonical spelling is refused when cited. A valid changed citation must not disappear behind complete/sourceComplete=true.

Actual: both spellings resolve to the same regular file, but literal string comparison skips the citation. An unfiltered invocation immediately detects the changed fragment.

Impact: changed-file-driven review misses affected tasks and their dependency/parent impact paths whenever a stored source uses an accepted equivalent path spelling.

Suggested direction: define one canonical lexical relative-path identity for filesystem providers, and apply it to producers, legacy stored descriptors, changed operands, and cache keys; alternatively reject noncanonical new operands and migrate/normalize old ones at comparison. Preserve traversal refusals and do not reinterpret arbitrary custom-provider identifiers without a provider contract. Add a built-SDK regression comparing full and filtered scans of the same changed file.

Duplicate check: searched all issue states for path, changed, and normalization. The unrelated closed distribution issue #20 is not this defect.
